# Manifest schema for bin/0mm-run (0mm-containers ADR 0002).
# bin/0mm-run reads this file. It is the one place the manifest keys are decided.
#
# A manifest is one TOML file per tool, in a strict subset: `key = value` lines,
# where a value is a "string" without escapes, true or false, an integer, or a
# one-line array of strings. Comments sit on their own lines. Anything else is refused.
#
# Columns: key, type (string|array|bool|int|-), presence (required|optional|forbidden), check.
# A key not listed here is refused as unknown. A forbidden key is refused as "not allowed".
#
# key          type    presence   check
runtime        string  required   runtime
image          string  required   digest
command        array   required   nonempty
network        string  optional   network
mounts         array   optional   mount
devices        array   optional   device
env            array   optional   envname
pids_limit     int     optional   -
memory         string  optional   size
cpus           string  optional   cpus
privileged     -       forbidden  -
cap_add        -       forbidden  -
security_opt   -       forbidden  -
userns         -       forbidden  -
pid            -       forbidden  -
ipc            -       forbidden  -
